From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vigaz <pudimdebacon3@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:30:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Show a GPU governor picker in the kernel manager

The GPU group only had min/max frequency; with TYPE_GPU_GOVERNOR now
provided by the kernel manager service, render it with the same
GovernorPreference the CPU clusters use. The composable only hardcoded
the CPU title, so it takes a title resource now and keeps the CPU one as
its default. The picker is skipped when the device exposes no GPU
governor node.

Change-Id: Ib72a9c17d9ca213d4d7be79caa1406356a75e610
---
 res/values/strings.xml                          |  1 +
 .../ui/screens/KernelManagerScreen.kt           | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/res/values/strings.xml b/res/values/strings.xml
index 84836f2..3f28287 100644
--- a/res/values/strings.xml
+++ b/res/values/strings.xml
@@ -417,6 +417,7 @@
     <string name="gpu">GPU</string>
     <string name="graphics_performance">Graphics Performance</string>
     <string name="cpu_governor">CPU governor</string>
+    <string name="gpu_governor">GPU governor</string>
     
     <!-- Performance Formats -->
     <string name="mhz_format">%1$d MHz</string>
diff --git a/src/com/android/axion/axionparts/ui/screens/KernelManagerScreen.kt b/src/com/android/axion/axionparts/ui/screens/KernelManagerScreen.kt
